  "behavior": {
    "purpose": "WorkItemStore.listTreeByWorkPackage captures display metadata beside actual rows. SQLite uses one synchronous transaction under the existing gate; Memory clones actual rows and scoped maps before any yield. Ordinary listByWorkPackage and structural history row shapes remain unchanged.",
    "projection": "Every current leaf receives steps:[{stepId,code,name,via}], including explicit empty lists. Direct types do not inherit. Retained type conflict resolves[] and preserves every actual typeId for rendering. Parents omit leaf metadata. Existing SC18 resolver preserves every matching provenance binding.",
    "integration": "Isolated service tree and SQLite captured live metadata consume the purpose. Actual mounted isolated/shared controls validate full provenance and untyped/retained-conflict behavior. New response field is optional for parents/older producers, never fabricated from package union.",
    "compatibility": "Refactored synchronous ordinary SQLite row selection retains SQL order and promised error protocol. Memory row cloning is shared without async port reentry. Existing capacity test now authors both actual team joins through patch rather than replacing the retired tree read path; original bound-team assertion remains. Final review found the live steps key could spread into current15/16document rows. documentWorkItems strips that derived field until the explicitSC9version/converter change. No version or frozen bytes changed."
  },
